it is a proxy (31 is an upper bound on real callers: a name can be shared), NOT a per-key verification.\n\nTHE QUESTION (a decision, not a bug until ruled): is a CI/lint tool in scripts/ a production caller for this gate? If yes, scanning scripts/ (the files are Python without a .py suffix; collect_production_references takes a file list, so the demotion arm can include them) would demote ~37 keys and shrink the baseline. If no, say so in the module docstring, so the baseline's script-called keys read as a decision rather than an artefact. Either way the 37 should stop being indistinguishable from the 8 unwired functions filed alongside this."  # 3536
